{"resourceIdentifier":"3425","resourceName":"Kwamisa/Other reserves community Forest Project","description":"The Project Activity is planting trees to restore the area, improve biodiversity, improve livelihoods of the local communities around the degraded forests and join the fight against climate change which has become a threat of global warming to the planet. The project will increase the sequestration capacity of carbon dioxide and other Greenhouse gases by increasing the forest and vegetative cover.\r\nThe project will contribute to the removal of GHG from the atmosphere. Through the plantation of teak, which is a wood biomass, its implemented on degraded forest reserve. Which without human influence and financial support will remain degraded, especially due to rapid depletion on and off-reserve stocks. This would lead to loss of carbon sinks and the negative climatical conditions will be evidence, impacting the social and economic activities of the region.\r\nThe carbon project will be managed by Private Afforestation Developers Organisation (PADO) which is an umbrella Organisation of private forest plantation developers in Ghana. They are the legal owners of the plantations located in Ghana; Kumasi at Kwamisa Forest Reserve located at Offinso Forest District within the Ashanti Region of Ghana. The reserve lies midway between Kumasi-Techiman and the Kumasi–Sunyani Road about 35 miles north of Kumasi.\r\nThe ARR activities are carried out and monitored according to approved project methodology AR-ACM0003 (Ver 2.0) for a project period of 40 years. The project expected to remove 26,281 t/CO2e annually and 1,051,223 tCO2e during its entire life.  The project has an goal to achieve forest plantations recovering 3010 hectares (ha) from degraded forest reserve in a total project zone of 5225 ha. The area was a degraded land Prior to the project implementation caused by a serious fire disaster in 1983 which engulfed Ghana and led to   massive forest degradation and severe hunger crisis.","location":{"latitude":6.963358,"longitude":1.975832},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-08-18","endExclusive":"2022-09-18","endInclusive":"2022-09-17"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3425"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ashanti Region"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3425"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3425"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"42252"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":4207}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3010 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"EPIC Sustainability Services Private Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/01/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 01/05/2019 - 30/04/2059"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=70026&IDKEY=m903q4jsafkasjfu90amnmasdfkaidflnmdf9348r09dmfasdf496565854","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"Ghana PD_150722 _ver01.pdf","uploadDate":"2022-07-15T06:53:22.153Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?F